-  "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept / precise-object-edit.\nAsset type: replacement square illustrated menu poster for Beat my track's 3\u00c3\u20143 racing challenge.\nEdit target and style reference: the supplied project poster. Redesign its composition to communicate exactly THREE TRACKS and exactly THREE TICKETS at a glance. Preserve its mature, crisp cel-shaded illustration language, restrained natural colours, navy outlines, believable asphalt, compacted desert sand and snow, fictional unbranded racing world. This is final in-game artwork, not a UI mockup.\n\nComposition: a beautifully composed square 1:1 illustration. In the upper roughly 75% show exactly THREE clearly separate miniature CLOSED-LOOP RACE CIRCUITS, each a complete readable loop with its own distinctive shape. Arrange them as three offset horizontal landscape dioramas, with enough separation to count all three instantly: top lush pine forest circuit on green ground, middle warm rocky DESERT circuit with a compacted tan SAND racing surface, bottom snowy alpine circuit on white ground with dark asphalt. Elevated high-oblique overhead view of the tracks, generous visible track surface, subtle landscape depth and clean graphic silhouettes; each loop has its own little black/white checkerboard start band. Natural scenery stays subordinate to the three distinct track shapes. No road joins one circuit to another, no extra loops, no split roads or crossing confusing tracks. Remove the large foreground cars and three-lamp starter boards from the source; the TRACKS are the subjects now.\n\nIn the lower foreground show exactly THREE large physical RACE ENTRY TICKETS, each separately countable, arranged side-by-side in a shallow slightly staggered fan across most of the image width, with minimal overlap. All three ticket outlines must be clearly visible: warm ivory paper, dark navy fine border, characteristic notched short edges, one dashed perforated tear-off stub, simple black/white checkered racing emblem, restrained amber highlights, subtle paper texture and cast shadows. Each ticket is a single rectangular paper object, no extra detached stubs. Make the tickets large enough to recognize at a small menu-card size. No hand holding them, no money, coins, credit cards, trophy, or extra objects.\n\nKeep every circuit and ticket fully inside the square frame with a modest safe margin. Strong readable hierarchy and cohesive polished game key art; no thin comic panel borders, no unnecessary decoration or large empty areas. Background is a dark muted navy atmosphere that unifies the three landscape islands and gives the ivory tickets contrast. Exactly THREE independent track loops + exactly THREE tickets, with all SIX subjects readable in the central 90% of the artwork. No lettering, titles, numbers, logos, manufacturer branding, watermark, interface or caption; game UI adds its own 3\u00c3\u20143 caption separately. Opaque background.",
